<Base title="Map credits & data sources"><section class="wrap credits"><a href="/places">← Back to the map</a><header class="page-head"><h1>Map credits</h1><p>The people and open data behind our maps.</p></header><h2>Map display and base map</h2><p><a href="https://maplibre.org/">MapLibre GL JS</a> is licensed under BSD-3-Clause; the <a href="/licences/maplibre-gl.txt">full licence and notices</a> are included with this site. Vector maps are provided by <a href="https://openfreemap.org/">OpenFreeMap</a>, using OpenMapTiles and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">© OpenStreetMap contributors</a>. Map attribution also appears in the map's attribution control. OpenStreetMap data is available under the Open Database Licence.</p><h2 id="terrain">Terrain elevations</h2><p>The <a href="https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/">Terrain Tiles open dataset</a> is managed by Mapzen, a Linux Foundation project, and hosted on AWS. Elevation sources have different resolutions and dates; heights are approximate.</p><ul><li>Mapzen.</li><li>ArcticDEM terrain data DEM(s) were created from DigitalGlobe, Inc., imagery and funded under National Science Foundation awards 1043681, 1559691, and 1542736.</li><li>Australia terrain data © Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia) 2017.</li><li>Austria terrain data © offene Daten Österreichs – Digitales Geländemodell (DGM) Österreich.</li><li>Canada terrain data contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence – Canada.</li><li>Europe terrain data produced using Copernicus data and information funded by the European Union – EU-DEM layers.</li><li>Global ETOPO1 terrain data: U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration.</li><li>Mexico terrain data source: INEGI, Continental relief, 2016.</li><li>New Zealand terrain data Copyright 2011 Crown copyright (c) Land Information New Zealand and the New Zealand Government (All rights reserved).</li><li>Norway terrain data © Kartverket.</li><li>United Kingdom terrain data © Environment Agency copyright and/or database right 2015. All rights reserved.</li><li>United States 3DEP (formerly NED) and global GMTED2010 and SRTM terrain data courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey.</li></ul><p>See the <a href="https://github.com/tilezen/joerd/blob/master/docs/attribution.md">dataset attribution and individual licences</a> for details.</p><h2>Place search and outdoor layers</h2><p>Place search uses <a href="https://github.com/komoot/photon">Photon</a> with OpenStreetMap data. Optional hiking, mountain biking, alpine routes, climbing sites, ski pistes/lifts and accommodation are queried from the public <a href="https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Overpass_API">Overpass API</a>. These are community-mapped features, not verified itineraries, bookable accommodation or current access/safety information. Search terms and requested map areas are sent to the relevant service. Provider caching and rate limits apply.</p><h2>Private GPX previews</h2><p>Imported GPX tracks remain in the current browser view. This map does not upload the GPX file or automatically publish its track. Map and elevation providers receive normal network requests for the area being viewed. Track distance and ascent are approximate and depend on the file's sampling and elevation quality.</p></section></Base>
